output:  MON1-32k-boot-rom.s19
0001                         *----------------------------------------------------------
0002                         * 32 byte Boot rom code for MON1 board of Newbear 77-68
0003                         * from MON1 board manual
0004                         *
0005                         * This program puts the first 1024 bytes to be received
0006                         * by ACIA(a) into the top 1k of RAM
0007                         *
0008                         * To start : hit `RESET` with system set to `BOOT`
0009                         * When finished, `RUN` lamp goes out
0010                         *
0011                         * As the 1k loaded should overwrite the RESET vector with
0012                         * the start addreess of the new code,
0013                         * then pressing RESET should start that program.
0014                         *
0015                         *----------------------------------------------------------
0016 ffe0                            ORG     $FFE0   * Start address for code
0017                         *
0018 ffe0 86 03              START   LDAA    #$03    * Reset
0019 ffe2 b7 f4 01                   STAA    $F401   *  ACIA(a)
0020 ffe5 86 11                      LDAA    #$11    * Set up ACIA
0021 ffe7 b7 f4 01                   STAA    $F401   *  control register
0022 ffea ce fc 00                   LDX     #$FC00  * Point to start of 1k RAM
0023 ffed 35                         TXS             * Point stack somewhere
0024 ffee b6 f4 01           LOOP    LDAA    $F401   * Read ACIA(a) control register
0025 fff1 85 01                      BITA    #$01    * If no data ready...
0026 fff3 27 f9                      BEQ     LOOP    *  look again
0027 fff5 b6 f4 00                   LDAA    $F400   * Get the data byte to A
0028 fff8 a7 00                      STAA    0,X     * Store it
0029 fffa 08                         INX             * Point to next RAM location
0030 fffb 26 f1                      BNE     LOOP    * If not done, then get next byte
0031 fffd 3e                         WAI             * Done ( 1K loaded ) kill RUN lamp
0032 fffe ff e0                      FDB     #START  * Put start address in RESET vector
0033                         *
0034                         *       The end
0035                         *----------------------------------------------------------
